## 4. P08 lambda-contract sites (condition: reseed intact)

`functionLiteral`'s seeding `currentReturnType = Context.follow(f.t)` (TFunc.t = the
lambda's own return contract) is untouched by the patch, and all return-position readers
still read `currentReturnType`. Functional check with a constructed probe
(`evidence/lam-probe/Lam.hx`): member `pick(flag:Bool):Int` calls `use(f:Void->ReadOnlyArray<Int>)`
with a **multi-statement lambda body** (local, then switch-bound local, then `return`) —
per the known trap, a single-statement `return try {…}` shape is refused at generation,
so the body was made multi-statement. Post-patch generation emits
`Lam.use({ () -> ReadOnlyArray<Int32> in … })`: the closure header takes the **lambda's
own contract** (`ReadOnlyArray<Int32>`), not the enclosing member's `Int32` — the P08
reseed survives. Trees base↔post byte-identical; `swiftc -c` rc=0.
Caveat: verified by generation + compile, not by per-site instrumented type readings
(the source report's SEVTRACE method was not re-run here); the cited line numbers
:810/:5296/:5310/:5675 shifted by the patch's +6/+2 offsets, sites confirmed present by
inspection (TReturn→`switchReturn(..., currentReturnType)` at ~:813; `armLines`
destination pass-through at ~:5681).

